  "language_probability": 1,
  "text": "This washing machine removes water from wet clothes by spinning the drum rapidly. The clothes stay against the drum wall while water escapes. The drum wall pushes inward on the clothes to keep them moving in a circle. Water is not held in the same way, so it can move outward through the fabric. The drum's small holes let that water pass into the outer tub. A pump then drains the water away while the clothes stay inside the perforated drum. A balanced load keeps the drum stable and lets it reach an effective spin speed. So rotation, perforations and drainage remove water without squeezing the clothes.",
